      "writtenOn": "2022-07-20T04:08:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i don\u0027t think it\u0027s simpler.  stat has no side-effects.  open updates the file descriptor table.  iiuc, that makes it more expensive to process in the kernel. in a multithread/multiprocess situation, this also opens it to leaks.  if this code were used only in the context of `minijail_run`, that might be a bit forgivable, but this shows up when simply constructing the minijail state.\n\nbasically, as a library, imo we should be opening file descriptors only when necessary, and in this case, it looks like lstat should suffice.",
